## 2. Market Leader Architecture: What, Why & How
| Dimension | What They Used | Why They Used It (Drivers & Bottlenecks) | How To Implement It (Concrete Mechanics) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Geospatial Tier** | Uber H3 / Google S2 | Avoids relational table scans; constant-time neighbor cell lookup; distortion-free indexing | Index GPS to H3 Resolution 8 cells; store driver sets in Redis Sets keyed by cell ID |
| **Ingress & Streaming** | WebSockets / gRPC + Kafka | Ultra-low latency duplex location pings; high-throughput append-only event log | Drivers stream location pings via WebSockets to Ingress Gateway; Ingress pushes to Kafka `driver.locations.v1` |
| **Concurrency Guard** | Redis Mutex (`SET NX EX` / Redlock) | Eliminates race condition where multiple drivers accept the same ride | Acquire 5s TTL distributed lock on `lock:ride:{rideId}` before dispatching confirmation |
| **State Machine** | Event-Driven Saga | Microservice boundaries require eventual consistency without distributed 2PC locks | Saga orchestrator coordinates Ride State &rarr; Payment Authorization &rarr; Receipt Generation |
| **Persistence** | PostgreSQL + PostGIS & ScyllaDB | Relational ACID safety for accounts & billing; wide-column store for telemetry & history | Active trips in Redis + PostgreSQL; completed trip coordinates archived into ScyllaDB |

